  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "For an **upper-upscale hotel positioning strategy in Europe**, an owner should primarily consider **brands with a proven upper-upscale classification and strong European footprint**. The clearest branded options in the search results are **Radisson Blu**, **Autograph Collection**, and **25hours Hotel**; broader upper-upscale/luxury-adjacent choices in Europe also include **Marriott Hotels**, **Hilton Hotels & Resorts**, **Sheraton**, **Hyatt Regency**, **InterContinental**, **Sofitel**, **NH Collection**, and **Kempinski**.[1][2][4][6][12][15]\n\nThe most directly supported upper-upscale brands from the results are:\n\n- **Radisson Blu** — identified as Europe’s largest upper-upscale hotel brand, with 186 hotels and almost 45,000 rooms in operation in one cited ranking.[1][4]\n- **Autograph Collection** — listed by STR/CoStar as an **Upper Upscale Chain**.[2]\n- **25hours Hotel** — also listed by STR/CoStar as an **Upper Upscale Chain**.[2]\n- **Wyndham Grand** — described as an upscale/upper-upscale brand in the results, and commonly used as a positioning option for this segment.[6][13][14]\n- **Marriott Hotels** / **Hilton Hotels & Resorts** / **Sheraton** / **Hyatt Regency** / **InterContinental** / **Sofitel** — these are repeatedly grouped in the results as upscale-to-upper-upscale brands that fit premium business and leisure positioning in Europe.[5][6][15]\n\nIf the goal is specifically an **upper-upscale positioning strategy in Europe**, the practical shortlist is:\n\n- **Radisson Blu**\n- **Autograph Collection**\n- **25hours Hotel**\n- **Wyndham Grand**\n- **Marriott Hotels**\n- **Hilton Hotels & Resorts**\n- **Sheraton**\n- **Hyatt Regency**\n- **InterContinental**\n- **Sofitel**\n- **NH Collection**\n- **Kempinski**[1][2][5][6][12][15]\n\nFor an owner, the final brand choice usually depends on whether the asset is best suited to a **conversion-friendly soft brand** or a **classic full-service premium brand**. The results suggest that **Autograph Collection** and **25hours** are attractive for conversion and lifestyle positioning, while **Radisson Blu**, **Marriott Hotels**, **Hilton Hotels & Resorts**, and **InterContinental** are stronger if the strategy is a conventional full-service upper-upscale flag with broad recognition.[2][4][6][15]\n\nIf you want, I can turn this into a **Europe-specific owner shortlist** by segmenting the brands into **conversion-friendly**, **business-destination**, and **resort/leisure** options.",
